1
00:00:05,596 --> 00:00:07,689
You need any help
getting that to the table?

2
00:00:07,865 --> 00:00:09,856
I have an extremely high metabolism rate.

3
00:00:10,034 --> 00:00:13,094
- Yeah, that'd be my guess.
- It was worse when I was growing up.

4
00:00:13,271 --> 00:00:16,138
For breakfast, Mom would have to fix
me a few dozen eggs...

5
00:00:16,307 --> 00:00:18,468
...and a couple of pounds of bacon.

6
00:00:18,643 --> 00:00:21,134
My whole family lived in constant fear.

7
00:00:22,380 --> 00:00:24,541
- Of what?
- Grease fire.

8
00:00:26,784 --> 00:00:29,617
- Don't take that pudding.
- Carla, there's plenty more.

9
00:00:29,787 --> 00:00:31,618
No, I mean don't buy it.

10
00:00:31,789 --> 00:00:34,723
I got an extra. You can have it.

11
00:00:34,891 --> 00:00:37,223
You got an extra bread pudding?

12
00:00:37,427 --> 00:00:40,919
I bought two. I guess my eyes
are bigger than my...

13
00:00:41,097 --> 00:00:43,759
Why don't you let me fill that part in?

14
00:00:44,034 --> 00:00:46,525
- You're so clever.
- Yeah, I guess I am.

15
00:00:46,703 --> 00:00:48,034
Well, bye.

16
00:00:48,204 --> 00:00:50,104
Bye. Thanks, Carla.

17
00:00:50,273 --> 00:00:53,208
- I paid for it.
- That's a switch.

18
00:00:56,780 --> 00:00:58,873
"Why don't you let me fill that part in?"

19
00:00:59,049 --> 00:01:02,678
- I beg your pardon?
- Oh, "you're so clever."

20
00:01:03,086 --> 00:01:04,348
Something bugging you?

21
00:01:04,521 --> 00:01:07,285
Harry, how could you take pudding
from a hooker?

22
00:01:09,292 --> 00:01:12,193
I never thought anyone
would ask me that question.

23
00:01:12,362 --> 00:01:14,091
You're a judge.

24
00:01:14,264 --> 00:01:16,562
- It's improper.
- Oh, come on.

25
00:01:16,733 --> 00:01:19,896
She's been in our court every day
and she's not even on the docket.

26
00:01:20,070 --> 00:01:23,039
- So?
- And you know, there's been a fresh rose...

27
00:01:23,206 --> 00:01:25,105
...every night on your bench too.

28
00:01:25,274 --> 00:01:26,901
I noticed. Thanks.

29
00:01:27,076 --> 00:01:30,876
You thought l... That's a laugh.

30
00:01:31,046 --> 00:01:32,980
From me, he thought, you see...

31
00:01:33,148 --> 00:01:36,049
Excuse me, could you hurry it up?

32
00:01:36,218 --> 00:01:39,346
I don't want my fish sticks to get cold.

33
00:01:40,189 --> 00:01:42,054
There's nothing on your plate.

34
00:01:42,224 --> 00:01:44,158
They're in my pocket.

35
00:01:46,228 --> 00:01:48,355
I couldn't take any chances.

36
00:01:53,202 --> 00:01:55,136
- Oh, hi, Dan.
- Hi, Dan.

37
00:01:55,304 --> 00:01:56,669
What's the matter with you?

38
00:01:57,072 --> 00:01:58,699
I am depressed.

39
00:01:58,874 --> 00:02:00,102
Who wouldn't be?

40
00:02:00,309 --> 00:02:04,177
International crises threaten us
with the possibility of nuclear holocaust...

41
00:02:04,346 --> 00:02:07,042
...and the increase in violent crime
has raised the odds...

42
00:02:07,216 --> 00:02:09,343
...one of us is gonna
be murdered tonight.

43
00:02:09,518 --> 00:02:11,748
That ought to perk him up.

44
00:02:11,987 --> 00:02:14,182
- Hi, gang.
- Hi, judge.

45
00:02:14,356 --> 00:02:16,381
- Oh, hi, judge.
- Oh, Dan, Dan, look at this.

46
00:02:16,558 --> 00:02:19,390
You'll love this. Squirting flower.
Just 59 cents.

47
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:21,892
They're having a big sale
at the novelty shop.

48
00:02:22,063 --> 00:02:25,794
Wow, thanks.
I better get right down there.

49
00:02:26,367 --> 00:02:29,200
- Dan, are you all right?
- He's got the blues.

50
00:02:29,504 --> 00:02:30,937
I don't get the blues.

51
00:02:31,105 --> 00:02:34,597
Jelly Roll Morton gets the blues.

52
00:02:34,909 --> 00:02:37,537
I get devastated.

53
00:02:38,312 --> 00:02:40,872
- The returns must be coming in now, huh?
- Yes, they are.

54
00:02:41,048 --> 00:02:43,983
Oh, my God, I almost forgot.
The special election is tonight.

55
00:02:44,152 --> 00:02:46,484
You're up for a city council seat.

56
00:02:46,888 --> 00:02:48,719
You're losing.

57
00:02:49,524 --> 00:02:51,014
That's why you're depressed.

58
00:02:51,192 --> 00:02:54,161
Yes, I am losing,
but that's not the depressing part.

59
00:02:54,328 --> 00:02:57,456
Hey, didn't your opponent die
two weeks ago?

60
00:02:59,066 --> 00:03:01,830
That's the depressing part.

61
00:03:02,570 --> 00:03:06,700
So how bad are you?

62
00:03:06,874 --> 00:03:09,808
The body is ahead by 20 percent.

63
00:03:10,844 --> 00:03:14,439
Come on, Dan, you know how
unsophisticated the public is.

64
00:03:14,614 --> 00:03:18,175
They don't vote for issues.
They vote for personality.

65
00:03:23,256 --> 00:03:26,225
I've gotta make a call.

66
00:03:29,229 --> 00:03:30,594
Remember...

67
00:03:30,764 --> 00:03:35,133
...when alive was a good thing to be?

68
00:03:38,205 --> 00:03:40,139
I need a napkin. Anybody need anything?

69
00:03:40,307 --> 00:03:41,740
- No.
- A fork? Knife?

70
00:03:41,908 --> 00:03:44,604
Bull, standing rib roast?

71
00:03:44,945 --> 00:03:46,742
Be right back.

72
00:03:48,215 --> 00:03:50,342
- Need a glass of water?
- Oh, no, thanks, Carla.

73
00:03:50,517 --> 00:03:53,975
- I just need a napkin.
- Here. I got condiments too.

74
00:03:55,789 --> 00:03:58,280
Thanks. A napkin will do. Thanks a lot.

75
00:03:58,458 --> 00:04:00,050
- Your Honor?
- Yeah?

76
00:04:00,427 --> 00:04:04,988
I just wanna say that... Well, since
I started being brought up in front of you...

77
00:04:05,164 --> 00:04:09,066
...I have developed a tremendous respect
for our justice system.

78
00:04:09,235 --> 00:04:11,795
- Thanks.
- A very healthy respect.

79
00:04:11,971 --> 00:04:13,370
Yeah, I sense that.

80
00:04:13,539 --> 00:04:16,303
And I have a great deal
of respect for you too.

81
00:04:16,475 --> 00:04:19,137
- Well, yeah.
- Then, I've always been attracted...

82
00:04:19,311 --> 00:04:21,245
...to a man in a robe.

83
00:04:22,715 --> 00:04:25,275
That's a fairly common phenomenon.

84
00:04:25,451 --> 00:04:29,114
- Well, enjoy your pudding.
- I'm looking forward to it.

85
00:04:29,722 --> 00:04:34,750
Excuse me. Do you happen
to have a lint brush on you?

86
00:05:17,235 --> 00:05:21,228
Miss Williams, anything to say on your
defendant's behalf before I pass sentence?

87
00:05:21,406 --> 00:05:23,670
Your Honor, although my client
has pled guilty...

88
00:05:23,841 --> 00:05:26,537
...I sincerely hope
you'll express compassion...

89
00:05:26,711 --> 00:05:32,650
...for this pathetic, miserable, wretched,
empty shell of a human being.

90
00:05:32,817 --> 00:05:35,149
That's telling him.

91
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,820
The bench is overwhelmed with mercy.

92
00:05:37,989 --> 00:05:42,119
Let's make it 10 days suspended sentence,
and let's take a 10-minute recess.

93
00:05:42,293 --> 00:05:44,318
Your Honor, thank you.

94
00:05:45,363 --> 00:05:47,058
Oh, listen.

95
00:05:47,230 --> 00:05:51,132
I really appreciate what you did for me,
and I'd like to thank you.

96
00:05:51,301 --> 00:05:52,598
Don't mention it.

97
00:05:52,903 --> 00:05:56,737
Shall we say, over dinner?

98
00:05:58,709 --> 00:06:03,442
- What?
- You like seafood?

99
00:06:06,516 --> 00:06:09,144
- Your Honor...
- Harry. It's recess.

100
00:06:09,319 --> 00:06:13,779
Harry, I just wanted to say
that back there in the cafeteria...

101
00:06:13,957 --> 00:06:17,154
...well, maybe I got a little out of line.
- Oh, don't worry about that.

102
00:06:17,327 --> 00:06:20,023
No, I mean, heck, your personal life
is your personal life.

103
00:06:20,197 --> 00:06:22,495
And I don't wanna interfere in that.

104
00:06:22,666 --> 00:06:25,157
It's just, you know, a friendly warning.

105
00:06:25,335 --> 00:06:29,135
I mean, maybe I do get
a little overprotective at times.

106
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:34,801
It's just that your position is one of such
honor, and I feel that in some ways...

107
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:37,310
...you know, it's my responsibility and...

108
00:06:38,915 --> 00:06:41,212
Well, I just hope you understand.

109
00:06:41,884 --> 00:06:44,216
Thank you for listening.

110
00:06:49,091 --> 00:06:50,558
Judge?

111
00:06:51,327 --> 00:06:52,692
What's that?

112
00:06:52,928 --> 00:06:55,192
A green stick.

113
00:06:56,132 --> 00:06:59,124
- What can I do for you?
- I bought that champagne and other stuff.

114
00:06:59,835 --> 00:07:02,303
Are we still having
the victory celebration for Dan?

115
00:07:02,471 --> 00:07:05,702
Oh, sure. I think things will turn around
once all the returns are in.

116
00:07:05,875 --> 00:07:09,834
Okay. Oh, I bought white champagne.
Is that right?

117
00:07:10,513 --> 00:07:13,710
- Well, let's see. We're serving it with?
- Cheetos.

118
00:07:14,183 --> 00:07:15,707
Perfect.

119
00:07:20,222 --> 00:07:23,214
- Hello.
- Well, hello yourself.

120
00:07:23,392 --> 00:07:25,189
- Got a sec?
- What can I do for you?

121
00:07:25,561 --> 00:07:28,860
- That's what I was gonna ask you.
- Well, I asked you first.

122
00:07:29,265 --> 00:07:32,722
Your Honor, back in the cafeteria...

123
00:07:32,901 --> 00:07:34,994
Well, I was trying to tell you something.

124
00:07:35,170 --> 00:07:37,638
Oh, Carla, there's no need to.

125
00:07:37,806 --> 00:07:40,536
- There's not?
- No. We both know what's going on here.

126
00:07:40,709 --> 00:07:43,439
- Then you feel it too?
- Oh, no. Feel... I didn't say feel.

127
00:07:43,611 --> 00:07:48,412
No, l... I don't... I don't feel. I mean, I feel,
but I don't feel what you feel I feel.

128
00:07:48,583 --> 00:07:51,279
- You know what I mean?
- No, but I just love hearing you...

129
00:07:51,453 --> 00:07:54,752
...spout nonsense.
- Papers. Sign them.

130
00:07:54,923 --> 00:07:57,187
Thank you.
We'll talk later.

131
00:07:57,358 --> 00:08:00,122
- Great.
- I have to make some calls...

132
00:08:00,295 --> 00:08:04,095
...so I'm gonna go in here
since there's no phone out here.

133
00:08:04,265 --> 00:08:07,701
- That's precious.
- Yeah.

134
00:08:08,770 --> 00:08:10,169
Bye.

135
00:08:10,972 --> 00:08:12,769
What a guy.

136
00:08:13,007 --> 00:08:15,100
What were you two talking about?

137
00:08:15,343 --> 00:08:18,574
The judge and I were having
a personal discussion.

138
00:08:18,947 --> 00:08:20,209
How personal?

139
00:08:20,949 --> 00:08:23,110
What business is it of yours?

140
00:08:23,551 --> 00:08:25,074
You're right.

141
00:08:25,252 --> 00:08:29,621
You're right. It is none of my business.
But if you want a little friendly advice:

142
00:08:30,157 --> 00:08:31,488
Forget it.

143
00:08:31,658 --> 00:08:33,125
He's not your type.

144
00:08:35,095 --> 00:08:39,555
- But I suppose he's your type.
- He's a sensitive, intellectual, complex man.

145
00:08:39,733 --> 00:08:43,169
Eclectic in nature,
multidimensional in personality.

146
00:08:43,337 --> 00:08:48,400
And, well, frankly, he would need a woman
of similar qualities to stimulate him.

147
00:08:49,343 --> 00:08:51,573
Honey, I don't know what
those words mean...

148
00:08:51,745 --> 00:08:55,738
...but I do know
what it takes to please a man.

149
00:08:56,383 --> 00:08:58,908
Physical stimulation is not enough.

150
00:08:59,887 --> 00:09:02,412
I won't use gadgets.

151
00:09:05,926 --> 00:09:09,089
That's... That's not what I meant.

152
00:09:09,263 --> 00:09:12,323
You see, dear, most psychologists
and experts agree...

153
00:09:12,499 --> 00:09:15,900
...the way a man and a woman
primarily respond to each other is cerebral.

154
00:09:16,603 --> 00:09:19,196
- What?
- The brain.

155
00:09:19,372 --> 00:09:23,809
Sex takes place between the ears.
You need a bond.

156
00:09:24,010 --> 00:09:26,843
You need a map.

157
00:09:34,987 --> 00:09:36,784
It's open. No need to break it down.

158
00:09:38,391 --> 00:09:40,484
- Judge Stone?
- Yeah. Come on in.

159
00:09:40,660 --> 00:09:44,323
I was in session down the hall.
Just thought I'd stop by and say hello.

160
00:09:44,497 --> 00:09:47,955
- Judge Robert T. Willard.
- Nice to meet you. Hey, neat robe.

161
00:09:48,134 --> 00:09:50,830
- I beg your pardon?
- How do you keep those bottom pleats...

162
00:09:51,003 --> 00:09:52,231
...from crinkling up?

163
00:09:52,405 --> 00:09:58,742
Yes, well... Judge Stone. Some of
the other judges and I were talking...

164
00:09:58,911 --> 00:10:01,778
...and, well, we just wanted you to know
we're available.

165
00:10:01,948 --> 00:10:03,415
You mean for weddings and stuff?

166
00:10:03,583 --> 00:10:07,815
Weddings? Oh, that's very amusing.
Weddings.

167
00:10:07,987 --> 00:10:11,149
- So what do you mean "available"?
- We wanted you to... Please.

168
00:10:11,323 --> 00:10:13,814
We wanted you to know
that we were accessible...

169
00:10:13,992 --> 00:10:16,552
...if you have any questions,
need any advice.

170
00:10:16,728 --> 00:10:19,219
Thanks. Great. Can I get you a Fresca?

171
00:10:19,397 --> 00:10:20,989
- No, thank you.
- I love the stuff...

172
00:10:21,199 --> 00:10:24,168
...but it's a weird name, ain't it?
- Yes. Judge Stone...

173
00:10:24,336 --> 00:10:27,703
You know what's even weirder than that
is I once knew a guy named Fresca.

174
00:10:27,873 --> 00:10:30,569
Judge Stone, I really don't have
much time to...

175
00:10:30,742 --> 00:10:35,145
- Oh, I'm sorry. You were saying?
- I've heard a little about how you operate.

176
00:10:35,313 --> 00:10:37,577
A bit too unconventional, some say.

177
00:10:37,749 --> 00:10:40,775
- A bit of a maverick, perhaps.
- Thanks.

178
00:10:41,119 --> 00:10:46,147
- Harry, if I might call you Harry?
- Sure, Bob.

179
00:10:48,627 --> 00:10:54,122
Judge Stone, we are entrusted
with a lot of responsibilities in our job.

180
00:10:54,299 --> 00:10:56,859
And, quite frankly, a lot of power.

181
00:10:57,035 --> 00:11:02,836
Now, if we start making a lot of waves,
draw a lot of attention to ourselves...

182
00:11:06,844 --> 00:11:10,644
Well, before you know it,
some of that power could be taken away.

183
00:11:10,814 --> 00:11:12,714
Am I making myself clear?

184
00:11:12,917 --> 00:11:14,748
Don't rock the boat? Is that it?

185
00:11:14,919 --> 00:11:20,721
Harry, don't misunderstand me.
We just think of ourselves as a fraternity.

186
00:11:20,891 --> 00:11:24,588
A club, if you will.
A very exclusive club...

187
00:11:24,862 --> 00:11:27,558
...whose members care about each other.

188
00:11:27,731 --> 00:11:32,168
Harry, we want you to be a member
of that club.

189
00:11:37,441 --> 00:11:40,308
I got a lot of neat stuff for the clubhouse.

190
00:11:42,413 --> 00:11:45,473
Yes. Very good.

191
00:11:49,586 --> 00:11:52,885
I find the defendant guilty,
and the fine will be 50 bucks.

192
00:11:53,057 --> 00:11:55,923
See the bailiff on the way out, please.
Next case.

193
00:11:56,092 --> 00:12:00,028
- That's it, Your Honor.
- Then that's a wrap. Court's adjourned.

194
00:12:05,468 --> 00:12:06,901
More returns?

195
00:12:07,370 --> 00:12:10,965
- I assume your opponent is still...
- Dead. Yes.

196
00:12:12,709 --> 00:12:16,907
- How's it going?
- The cadaver's opened up its lead.

197
00:12:17,981 --> 00:12:19,209
I'm sorry.

198
00:12:19,615 --> 00:12:24,484
I just hope there's no afterlife
so he can't gloat.

199
00:12:25,888 --> 00:12:28,152
Yeah, well, keep a good thought.

200
00:12:28,691 --> 00:12:33,287
Dan, I know you know, but if it's
of any consolation, I voted for you.

201
00:12:33,463 --> 00:12:36,762
- Me too.
- Yeah. We all voted for you. Didn't we?

202
00:12:36,933 --> 00:12:38,696
- Right.
- Absolutely.

203
00:12:49,778 --> 00:12:52,440
A secret ballot is our most treasured right...

204
00:12:52,614 --> 00:12:54,912
...afforded us under the constitution,
you know.

205
00:12:57,886 --> 00:13:02,346
- Who'd you vote for?
- The right of privacy is a guarantee...

206
00:13:02,524 --> 00:13:05,118
...to ensure an open and free election.

207
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:07,260
Who'd you vote for?

208
00:13:08,130 --> 00:13:13,227
We are indebted to our Founding Fathers
for creating and granting us this privilege.

209
00:13:13,402 --> 00:13:16,633
Whom did you vote for?

210
00:13:17,172 --> 00:13:19,640
I voted for the best man.

211
00:13:21,043 --> 00:13:23,671
I knew it.

212
00:13:25,180 --> 00:13:30,015
Come on, kids, it's party time.
The refreshments are this way.

213
00:13:30,552 --> 00:13:33,783
Judge Stone, so glad I caught you
before you left.

214
00:13:33,955 --> 00:13:36,719
We're going in to listen
to the returns and have a drink.

215
00:13:36,892 --> 00:13:41,225
Oh, yes, Fielding. Stiff still whomping you?

216
00:13:43,564 --> 00:13:46,761
- Yes, sir. Thank you, sir.
- Won't you join us, Judge Willard?

217
00:13:46,934 --> 00:13:49,664
Well, just for a second.
I really came by to say...

218
00:13:49,837 --> 00:13:52,965
...that if I came on a little strong earlier,
I'd like to apologize.

219
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:57,236
Oh, forget it. We all come on
a little strong every once in a while.

220
00:13:57,511 --> 00:14:00,036
Surprise!

221
00:14:07,321 --> 00:14:10,688
- What are these people doing here?
- What are you doing here?

222
00:14:10,858 --> 00:14:13,793
- I was supposed to meet him.
- There's been a misunderstanding.

223
00:14:13,961 --> 00:14:15,895
What is going on here?
Who is this woman?

224
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:18,429
- You mean the hooker?
- Hooker?

225
00:14:18,732 --> 00:14:22,463
Yes. Hooker, prostitute, streetwalker,
whatever you wanna call it.

226
00:14:22,636 --> 00:14:24,263
Meretrix?

227
00:14:25,773 --> 00:14:27,673
Look it up.

228
00:14:29,143 --> 00:14:32,601
- You lied to me.
- Carla, I didn't lie. I never said a thing.

229
00:14:32,779 --> 00:14:35,839
- You told me to meet you in your office.
- You don't really think...

230
00:14:36,015 --> 00:14:38,313
...he'd meet a hooker in his office, do you?

231
00:14:38,618 --> 00:14:40,711
You wouldn't, would you?

232
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:43,818
Is that it? Everybody had their laughs?

233
00:14:43,990 --> 00:14:47,187
Everybody get a kick out of seeing
the tart make a fool of herself?

234
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,850
- Carla...
- Stay away from me!

235
00:14:49,028 --> 00:14:52,862
- Come on, get dressed and we'll talk.
- Oh, what's the matter? You embarrassed?

236
00:14:53,032 --> 00:14:55,500
Well, you ain't seen nothing yet.

237
00:14:56,269 --> 00:14:58,464
Hi, everybody. Sorry I'm late.

238
00:14:59,539 --> 00:15:01,700
There. I threw all my clothes
out the window.

239
00:15:01,941 --> 00:15:05,672
At most I was expecting charades.

240
00:15:06,746 --> 00:15:08,873
Harry, do something.

241
00:15:09,048 --> 00:15:11,175
She's right. This calls for positive action.

242
00:15:11,351 --> 00:15:13,751
- What do you suggest?
- Bailiff, take her.

243
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:17,356
Anybody comes near me,
I follow my clothes out. Understand?

244
00:15:17,624 --> 00:15:20,457
"Sex Party in Judge's Chambers
Turns Tragic."

245
00:15:20,627 --> 00:15:24,654
- Great headline, huh?
- Make me wanna read further.

246
00:15:26,865 --> 00:15:29,993
Well, come on, everybody,
don't just stand around. Let's party!

247
00:15:30,169 --> 00:15:32,069
Bar's open.

248
00:15:32,871 --> 00:15:36,773
That's the spirit.
Come on, people, enjoy yourselves.

249
00:15:36,942 --> 00:15:38,534
Do you mind if I make a phone call?

250
00:15:38,710 --> 00:15:41,611
- Whatever turns you on, honey.
- Thank you.

251
00:15:41,780 --> 00:15:45,341
Dan, how could you think of yourself
at a time like this?

252
00:15:46,118 --> 00:15:50,885
Because I have stood next to death,
and people liked him better.

253
00:15:53,492 --> 00:15:56,188
- Well, good luck, Stone.
- Nobody leaves or I jump!

254
00:15:56,361 --> 00:15:59,694
I'm not going to stand here
and be blackmailed by anyone.

255
00:15:59,865 --> 00:16:02,299
Get your pompous butt
back in here, Willard.

256
00:16:03,135 --> 00:16:06,798
Bull, if anyone tries to leave...

257
00:16:09,608 --> 00:16:11,735
Have a seat.

258
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:18,009
Harry, why don't I have a talk with her,
woman-to-woman?

259
00:16:18,182 --> 00:16:19,615
That might help.

260
00:16:21,886 --> 00:16:25,788
- All right, get down off of there.
- Nice start.

261
00:16:26,023 --> 00:16:29,857
- Well, if it isn't the little prude.
- I am not little.

262
00:16:30,828 --> 00:16:34,491
- Or a prude.
- You ever made love with the lights on?

263
00:16:34,732 --> 00:16:36,199
Of course I have.

264
00:16:36,434 --> 00:16:38,629
A dimmer doesn't count.

265
00:16:43,774 --> 00:16:45,708
Carla, please come out of the window.

266
00:16:45,876 --> 00:16:47,571
I wonder what it feels like to fly.

267
00:16:47,745 --> 00:16:50,270
You won't like it. Trust me.
You get bugs in your eyes.

268
00:16:50,448 --> 00:16:52,313
And pigeons push you around.

269
00:16:52,516 --> 00:16:55,644
Come on. You're wasting our time
standing there, fooling around.

270
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:59,312
I thought fooling around was preferable
to the alternative at this point.

271
00:16:59,490 --> 00:17:02,015
You aren't taking her seriously, are you?

272
00:17:02,193 --> 00:17:04,354
He's right. Nobody takes me seriously.

273
00:17:04,528 --> 00:17:05,893
Maybe it's time they did.

274
00:17:06,063 --> 00:17:08,395
A nose-dive in the middle
of downtown should do it.

275
00:17:08,566 --> 00:17:12,365
All right, Carla. Get the hell
inside that window and do it now!

276
00:17:12,535 --> 00:17:15,629
- Into the rough stuff, huh?
- Listen, I apologized.

277
00:17:15,805 --> 00:17:18,171
I offered to talk. What else can I do?

278
00:17:18,441 --> 00:17:21,604
For starters? You can get me a drink.

279
00:17:21,811 --> 00:17:24,837
Good idea. A drink. You come over here.
We'll sit down and talk.

280
00:17:25,015 --> 00:17:26,744
- Here.
- Here.

281
00:17:26,916 --> 00:17:28,315
- Here.
- There.

282
00:17:28,485 --> 00:17:30,953
I'll get champagne. Don't go away.

283
00:17:31,121 --> 00:17:34,249
Operator, please, keep trying.
There must be somebody there.

284
00:17:34,424 --> 00:17:36,984
It's the Fielding for City Council
Headquarters.

285
00:17:41,364 --> 00:17:44,822
Yes, the joker who's losing to the corpse.

286
00:17:47,504 --> 00:17:51,838
I'm sure he must be a real nerd.

287
00:17:53,610 --> 00:17:55,407
Carla, listen to me.

288
00:17:55,578 --> 00:17:59,571
I am truly sorry if I said
or did anything to mislead you.

289
00:17:59,749 --> 00:18:01,046
You did plenty, all right.

290
00:18:01,584 --> 00:18:04,780
- What did I do?
- What did you do? Oh, come on.

291
00:18:04,953 --> 00:18:07,387
Every time I came to court,
you smiled at me.

292
00:18:07,556 --> 00:18:09,490
You treated me with respect.

293
00:18:09,658 --> 00:18:12,354
You were generally concerned
with my welfare.

294
00:18:12,528 --> 00:18:14,120
Damn it. You were nice to me.

295
00:18:14,296 --> 00:18:16,594
Carla, for the most part,
I'm nice to everybody.

296
00:18:16,765 --> 00:18:20,394
Yeah? Well, you just better get it
in your head that everybody in this world...

297
00:18:20,569 --> 00:18:23,402
...ain't used to being treated nice.
And if they are...

298
00:18:23,572 --> 00:18:25,904
...it's because somebody
wants something from them.

299
00:18:26,075 --> 00:18:29,977
So when somebody treats you nice,
and they don't want anything from you...

300
00:18:30,145 --> 00:18:31,976
...you think they love you.

301
00:18:32,147 --> 00:18:33,910
I thought you loved me.

302
00:18:35,217 --> 00:18:37,549
I know I loved you.

303
00:18:40,689 --> 00:18:43,658
Come on, Stone,
this has gone on long enough.

304
00:18:43,826 --> 00:18:46,090
Take a look at her.
She's not going to jump.

305
00:18:46,261 --> 00:18:48,695
No. She never was.

306
00:18:48,864 --> 00:18:51,560
Then pull her down from there,
and let's get out of here.

307
00:18:51,734 --> 00:18:55,794
She's just an emotionally mixed-up woman
who thought you were in love with her.

308
00:18:56,137 --> 00:18:58,071
Maybe she's right.

309
00:18:58,706 --> 00:19:01,300
I'm sorry, what did he say?

310
00:19:01,576 --> 00:19:03,737
I said, maybe she's right.

311
00:19:04,612 --> 00:19:07,843
- Maybe I am in love with her.
- Harry, what are you doing?

312
00:19:08,015 --> 00:19:10,176
I'm trying to look at things realistically.

313
00:19:10,351 --> 00:19:14,685
I mean, I did treat her nice. Maybe
I treated her extra-nice. I don't know.

314
00:19:15,022 --> 00:19:16,922
Isn't that the thing about our feelings?

315
00:19:17,091 --> 00:19:19,924
No, operator, I don't mind.

316
00:19:22,363 --> 00:19:24,957
Sometimes you can't even make sense
out of your own.

317
00:19:25,133 --> 00:19:28,330
- Do you know what I mean?
- I do.

318
00:19:28,936 --> 00:19:32,804
We all do, especially about love.

319
00:19:33,574 --> 00:19:36,737
When do you fall in love with somebody?

320
00:19:37,245 --> 00:19:39,907
When do you think
you're in love with somebody?

321
00:19:40,148 --> 00:19:44,517
When do you start to love?
And when is it complete?

322
00:19:45,486 --> 00:19:47,818
I don't know any more about love
than the next guy.

323
00:19:47,989 --> 00:19:49,751
I don't know if anybody does.

324
00:19:50,056 --> 00:19:54,288
But I do know that if someone told me
that they loved you...

325
00:19:56,196 --> 00:19:58,721
...I wouldn't have to ask why.

326
00:20:11,178 --> 00:20:14,807
Your Honor, l... I just...

327
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:24,019
I always wanted to do that to somebody.

328
00:20:25,158 --> 00:20:29,686
- Stone, mind if I go now?
- Not at all, Judge Willard.

329
00:20:29,863 --> 00:20:32,195
Oh, by the way, about that club of yours?

330
00:20:32,365 --> 00:20:34,128
I don't really think I'm interested.

331
00:20:34,301 --> 00:20:37,327
I mean, you know, no secret
handshakes or anything.

332
00:20:37,737 --> 00:20:41,365
Judge Stone, I'm not really sure
you're fit to wear that robe.

333
00:20:42,875 --> 00:20:45,139
I think you're right.

334
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:53,108
Selma, can you help out a lady
in distress here?

335
00:20:53,285 --> 00:20:57,585
Honey, I've got some clothes in my locker
you can wear on the way home.

336
00:20:57,756 --> 00:20:59,018
What size are you?

337
00:20:59,191 --> 00:21:02,524
Seven. Extra-shriveled.

338
00:21:06,765 --> 00:21:08,858
Listen, everybody.

339
00:21:09,235 --> 00:21:13,296
I wanna apologize
for acting like a real fool.

340
00:21:13,506 --> 00:21:17,101
Oh, no. Forget it.
It could have happened to any of us.

341
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:19,710
Well, most any of us.

342
00:21:20,145 --> 00:21:22,272
Judge Stone...

343
00:21:24,650 --> 00:21:26,880
Thanks for the dignity.

344
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:29,385
Thanks for the pudding.

345
00:21:36,761 --> 00:21:39,457
<i>All the precincts have now reported in,
and it's official.</i>

346
00:21:39,631 --> 00:21:45,592
<i>The 13th district city council seat
has been won by the late Edward Barnes.</i>

347
00:21:45,770 --> 00:21:49,604
<i>Barnes, who would have been 52
next January, pulled off a stunning upset...</i>

348
00:21:49,774 --> 00:21:54,211
<i>...in what many insiders felt was a sure bet
for the live candidate.</i>

349
00:21:54,379 --> 00:21:57,871
<i>That candidate, assistant district attorney
Dan Fielding, ha...</i>

350
00:21:59,450 --> 00:22:00,781
Sorry, Dan.

351
00:22:00,952 --> 00:22:05,514
So am I, Dan. I really am.

352
00:22:08,860 --> 00:22:11,158
You know, I think this just goes
to show you...

353
00:22:11,329 --> 00:22:13,456
...how really uninformed the public is.

354
00:22:13,631 --> 00:22:18,694
Why, I bet they didn't even know
the man they were voting for was dead.

355
00:22:19,404 --> 00:22:21,269
They knew.

356
00:22:22,373 --> 00:22:24,534
They knew.

357
00:22:24,909 --> 00:22:27,570
- The cake?
- Oh, here it is.

358
00:22:31,148 --> 00:22:32,581
- What's that?
- You'll see.

359
00:22:32,749 --> 00:22:35,115
Well, we had reason to believe you'd win.

360
00:22:35,285 --> 00:22:38,277
In any case, we just wanted to show you
how we felt about you.

361
00:22:38,455 --> 00:22:40,013
There's writing on it.

362
00:22:47,130 --> 00:22:50,622
"Dan, Dan, he's our man.

363
00:22:50,801 --> 00:22:55,170
If he can't do it, no body can."

364
00:22:59,743 --> 00:23:01,973
That's very touch...

365
00:23:05,916 --> 00:23:07,679
Thank you.

366
00:23:08,418 --> 00:23:09,749
I'll treasure it always.

